From c4157c262a69bf1f9726b59eb7922a7f63db039f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UCU map kit <ucu-map-kit@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:12:23 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat(export): GUIDs from an asset's identity in the game
 files

AssetRipper gives every exported asset a random GUID (`UnityGuid.NewGuid()` in AssetExportCollection), so two exports of
different level selections disagree on the assets they share. The GUID is now the MD5 of a key built from the asset's
identity:

- `file/<file name>/<path ID>` for an asset read from a game file;
- `processed/<collection>/<class ID>/<directory>/<name>` for an asset AssetRipper generates;
- `scene/<level file name>` for a scene with no GUID of its own.

A generated prefab takes its root GameObject's identity. A hash collision between two keys appends `#n`. The CLI writes
`AuxiliaryFiles/guid_map.tsv` (path, GUID, kind, key). Code GUIDs (scripts, assemblies) were already deterministic.
